## Build 3 cuts LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike from ~20 s/eval to few milliseconds at UNCHANGED accuracy (no tolerance widening). Measured facts: the engine call `_amplification_coefficients` is 99.3% of the ~20 s; it evaluates the Chang-Refsdal engine at 506 points/eval (253 bins x kernel_subsamples=2, the kernel grid inheriting the waveform bin grid), and per-point cost ~38 ms is dominated by the pure-Python double-double 1F1 derivative ladder. Within one eval the lens params are FIXED and only w=xi*f varies; the geometry/delays are computed once and are w-independent, so the per-eval work is really producing one smooth 1D curve K_a(w) sampled at bin centers. Both the Professor and the Simplifier converged on a two-lever, two-WP design: (WP1, lever 1 'cheap evals') numba-JIT the EXISTING double-double 1F1 ladder and the operator contraction loop so per-engine-point cost drops ~100x to <1 ms, keeping the same algorithm (F001 two-channel model and F005 refusal thresholds untouched, DD stays the oracle); (WP2, lever 2 'fewer evals') evaluate the engine on a coarse cubic-spline w-node grid (~8-12 deterministic nodes: log-spaced UNION the smootherstep transition frequencies) decoupled from the waveform bin grid, spline the smooth channel kernels K_a(w) to the 506 bin sub-samples, keeping image-delay phases analytic. Both consults REJECTED a 2D precomputed surrogate table as lever 1 (85 derivatives spanning ~100 orders of magnitude; certifying 2D interpolation to 1e-10 is research-grade and carries F002 oracle-tautology risk) and deferred it to a possible Build 3b only if numba proves insufficient. Lever 3 (contraction subdominance) is left as conditional cleanup per the brief: the server contraction is already 1.6 ms, so few-ms is reachable without it; if the 10 ms timing ceiling is missed after WP1+WP2, njit'ing `_data_term`/`_norm_term` is the Build 3b follow-up. ASSUMPTIONS (documented, non-interactive): (a) numba delivers >=100x on the DD inner loops (Professor high-confidence; if only ~50x, per-point ~0.8 ms still clears the 10 ms ceiling at ~10 nodes); (b) node placement is FIXED/deterministic per parameter point, never error-adaptive (Simplifier hard requirement); (c) a lightweight frequency-independent real-image-delay accessor is added to the engine so the likelihood can place transition nodes without paying an extra expensive engine call. POST-BUILD (doc-sync phase, not a WP): FINDINGS gains the measured surrogate story (chosen node count, measured per-point cost, interpolation-error calibration) sourced from the WP1/WP2 change reports; todo fragment engine_hyp1f1-surrogate.md retired. No DATA_CONTRACTS artifact is touched (the lensing likelihood is not a registered producer/consumer), so no producer->consumer ordering applies.

### WP1: numba-accelerate the Chang-Refsdal per-point engine (1F1 ladder + operator contraction)
  What: Make each engine evaluation point ~100x cheaper by JIT-compiling the pure-Python hot loops with numba, WITHOUT changing the algorithm, the numerical results (to <=2 ULP), the F001 two-channel double-double error model, or the F005 refusal contract. Target: per-engine-point cost drops from ~38 ms to <1 ms warm.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/_dd.py (scalar dd primitives), cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/_hyp1f1.py (`_shared_numerator`, `_ladder_sum`, and the k-ladder core of `point_mass_g_derivatives`), cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/operator.py (`F_op` order-accumulation loop).
  How: Draw the numba boundary so ALL exception-raising, threshold, and special-function logic stays in Python and only pure float64/complex128 arithmetic loops are JIT'd. Specifically: (1) In `_hyp1f1.py`, add `@numba.njit(cache=True, fastmath=False)` kernels for the shared-numerator recurrence and the reciprocal-binomial ladder sum (the loops currently in `_shared_numerator` and `_ladder_sum`), plus a njit core that runs the k=0..max_derivative ladder producing `values` and `relative_tail`. Keep `prefactor_c` (which calls scipy.special.loggamma, NOT numba-supported) and the phase-reduction/`_carrier` scalar setup in Python; PRECOMPUTE the complex `carrier` and the `ladder`/`base`/`a_parameter` prefactors in Python and pass them into the njit core (or compute the ladder prefactor inside njit since it is pure complex arithmetic). Preserve the exact dd recurrences, the measured per-k `relative_tail` diagnostic, and the domain validation (`_validate_domain` stays in Python before the njit call). (2) In `_dd.py`, decorate the scalar dd primitives (`dd_mul`, `dd_div`, `dd_add`/`dd_sub`, `dd_complex_mul`, `dd_complex_add`, etc.) with `@numba.njit(cache=True, fastmath=False)` so they inline into the njit kernels; DO NOT change their arithmetic (two-sum/two-product structure is load-bearing). fastmath MUST be False to preserve IEEE semantics and the cancellation-law error bound. (3) In `operator.py`, extract the `for order in range(max_order+1)` accumulation loop of `F_op` (the `z_powers @ (table[order]*radial) @ zbar_powers` contraction, the all-positive companion `positive_total`, `max_term`, `order_used`, `last_ratio`, `converged`) into a `@numba.njit(cache=True, fastmath=False)` function returning those scalars, with the small (dim=85) matmuls written as explicit loops. Keep OUTSIDE njit and BIT-UNCHANGED: `_mass_sheet_map`, the `np.frexp`/`np.ldexp` power-of-two rescaling, ALL four CancellationError refusal checks and their thresholds (`_CANCELLATION_REFUSAL`, `_CONTRACTION_TARGET`, `_CONTRACTION_GUARD`, non-finite backstops), and the final mass-sheet/phase reconstruction. Do NOT numba-compile `_exact_total`'s frequency loop (after WP2 it runs only ~10 points; leaving it in Python keeps the branch-select/exception plumbing simple). Numba compilation happens once at import/first-call (warm cost, not per-eval). Verify no `object mode` fallback (use `njit`, not `jit`).
  Who: Coder
  Verification: The numba-accelerated `point_mass_g_derivatives` and `F_op` are pure JIT re-expressions of the shipped algorithm: they agree with the mpmath-based oracles in the existing test_lensing_hyp1f1.py and test_lensing_operator.py suites at the ORIGINAL tolerances (rel ~1e-10 out to w*sqrt(s)~50), all four F005 CancellationError refusal paths and their thresholds are byte-for-byte unchanged and still fire on the same inputs, MacroMagnificationLimitTestCase stays green (rel 7.85e-9 at w down to 1e-12, tiny-w early-exit handled), no numba object-mode fallback occurs, and fastmath is False so results match the pre-numba values to <=2 ULP. Repeated calls are bit-identical (pure function). No tolerance is widened anywhere.
  Max turns: 105

### WP2: coarse cubic-spline kernel node grid decoupled from the waveform bin grid
  What: Stop evaluating the engine at all 506 bin sub-sample points. Instead evaluate it at a coarse, deterministic ~8-12-node w grid, cubic-spline the smooth channel kernels K_a(w) to the 506 bin sub-sample frequencies, and feed the interpolated kernels into the existing (k0,k1) reduction and contraction. Image-delay phases stay analytic and exact. Combined with WP1 this reaches few-ms/eval.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py (`_amplification_coefficients`, plus a new coarse-node-grid helper and the `LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.__init__` signature) and a small frequency-independent delay accessor in cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/channels.py.
  How: (1) Add a lightweight helper (module function or small `ChangRefsdalChannels` method) that returns the FREQUENCY-INDEPENDENT sorted real-image relative Fermat delays for given (gamma, y, beta, kappa), reusing `geometry.macro_matrix`/`geometry.find_images`/`geometry.delay` ONLY (NO `F_op`, no expensive per-w work). This lets the likelihood place nodes without paying an extra engine sweep. (2) In the likelihood, build the coarse w-node grid DETERMINISTICALLY (never error-adaptive): the sorted unique UNION of (a) a log-spaced base grid of `n_kernel_nodes` points over the in-band [w_min, w_max] = xi*[f_min, f_max] of the existing dense sub-sample grid, and (b) the mandatory transition frequencies {0.5/Delta_j, 4.0/Delta_j} for each distinct pairwise real-image delay separation Delta_j that falls in-band, plus the branch node 4.0/Delta_min if in-band. These transition frequencies are the C2-but-not-C3 kink locations of the smootherstep gauge hand-over (RHO_START=0.5, RHO_END=4.0) and the wave->geometric branch switch; placing nodes exactly there lets a cubic spline break at the regularity boundary and avoids ringing. Guarantee the grid is strictly positive and strictly increasing (ChangRefsdalChannels validates this). (3) Evaluate `ChangRefsdalChannels(coarse_w).evaluate(...)` ONCE; read `partition.delays` (frequency-independent, used analytically as today) and `partition.kernels` shape (n_node, n_channels). (4) Cubic-spline each channel kernel's real and imaginary parts SEPARATELY vs w using scipy.interpolate.CubicSpline (bc_type='not-a-knot'); evaluate the splines at the dense bin sub-sample w-grid (`self._kernel_dense_f` mapped through `dimensionless_frequency`) to get K_a at all 506 points, a vectorized microsecond operation. Handle the channel count generically (no per-eval Python branching on which channels are real; virtual channels carry zeros and spline to zeros harmlessly). (5) Feed the interpolated (n_bins, n_sub, n_channels) kernels into the EXISTING `_kernel_fit_value`/`_kernel_fit_slope` least-squares reduction unchanged, so the (k0,k1) contraction, moments, and `F->1` normalization are byte-for-byte the same downstream. (6) Add a public constructor kwarg `n_kernel_nodes` (default chosen ~8-12 to clear the 1e-8 interpolation gate with margin; document it alongside `kernel_subsamples`). Keep `kernel_subsamples` and the ratio path (`_edge_linear_coefficients`) unchanged. Engine refusals (`geometry.LensDomainError`, `operator.CancellationError`) must still propagate unswallowed and SYMMETRICALLY with `lnlike_bruteforce`. Do NOT touch the stall-ringdown/template builders, the delay-phase analytic model, `_validate_bin_delay_criterion`, or any refusal threshold.
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: `_amplification_coefficients` evaluates the engine only at the coarse `n_kernel_nodes`-plus-transition grid (order ~10, not 506), cubic-splines K_a(w) to the bin sub-samples, and leaves the delays analytic and the (k0,k1) reduction/contraction/normalization downstream byte-for-byte unchanged; node placement is deterministic per parameter point (log-spaced union mandatory transition/branch frequencies), never error-adaptive; the reconstructed F(f)=sum_a exp(i*w*tau_a)*K_a from the interpolated kernels matches the direct dense-engine evaluation to relative <1e-8 on the crown 4-image and other swept configs; the crown RB-vs-brute agreement holds at the ORIGINAL RB_ATOL=1.5; the F->1 zero-noise floor stays at 1e-2; warm best-of-5 `lnlike` on the crown config is at or under 10 ms (target few-ms) on the server; engine refusals propagate symmetrically on the RB and brute paths. No tolerance widened.
  Max turns: 90

### Professor Inputs
  - Confirmed the structural claim line-by-line: geometry/labels/delays in ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate are w-INDEPENDENT (computed once from macro_matrix/find_images/delay); the only w-dependent expensive work is _exact_total's per-frequency F_op loop, so the per-eval task is producing one smooth 1D curve K_a(w). Lever 2 (coarse node grid on K_a, splined to bins, delays analytic) is the correct PRIMARY mechanism.
  - K_a(w) is C2 but NOT C3: the smootherstep gauge hand-over (6u^5-15u^4+10u^3, RHO_START=0.5, RHO_END=4.0) has a discontinuous third derivative at the joins w=0.5/Delta_j and w=4.0/Delta_j, and there is a residual ~1/w^3 kink at the wave->geometric branch switch w=4/Delta_min. => Use a CUBIC SPLINE (matches the C2 regularity; a global Chebyshev would ring) with MANDATORY nodes AT those transition frequencies plus a log-spaced base grid; ~8-12 nodes reach ~1e-10 relative interpolation of K_a over a 1-2 decade in-band w range.
  - Recommended lever 1 = numba-compile the existing DD ladder + operator contraction, NOT a 2D table. The 85-derivative output spans ~100 orders of magnitude and certifying its 2D interpolation to 1e-10 (accounting for the cancellation) is a research problem with high silent-corner risk; numba preserves exact accuracy, F001's two-channel model, and F005's refusal contract by construction. Expected ~0.2-0.4 ms/point post-numba => ~5-6 ms combined with lever 2 (few-ms). If numba lands at only ~50x, njit'ing the contraction recovers margin; a 2D table is the <20%-probability Build 3b escalation.
  - Test tolerances carry the Professor's authority: numba-vs-oracle at relative ~1e-10 judged against an INDEPENDENT mpmath reference (NOT the code itself - F002), preserving the pre-numba cancellation-law envelope; coarse-node interpolation gate at relative 1e-8 on the RECONSTRUCTED F(f) (not individual K_a, which are only defined up to label permutation, and not lnlike, which would conflate with the RB binning floor) vs a direct dense-engine oracle; this sits 100x inside both the 1e-10 DD accuracy and the RB_ATOL=1.5 lnlike gate while staying above the ~1e-4 physical binning floor.
  - The non-negotiable crown gates that must stay green unchanged through the fast path: RB-vs-brute at RB_ATOL=1.5 on the crown 4-image config, the F->1 zero-noise floor at 1e-2 (the fast path must REPRODUCE the F007/F009 stall-ringdown construction floor, not remove it), MacroMagnificationLimitTestCase at rel 7.85e-9 down to w=1e-12 (numba must preserve tiny-w early-exit), and the near-cusp deterministic pin (F008 switch fix). A warm best-of-5 lnlike <=10 ms absolute ceiling on the crown config is a sound in-build timing gate (public entry point, one eval, deterministic, brute-force-free).

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - COARSE-NODE INTERPOLATION GATE (new; the brief's surrogate-vs-oracle gate, lever 2). Setup: construct the LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood on the crown 4-image seeded fixture (y=(0.08,0.06), gamma=0.20, kappa=beta=0, M_lens/z_lens per the suite) and a small handful of additional lens configs drawn from the existing _LENS_CONFIGS (2-image, near-fold, kappa!=0). Operation: for each config, build the coarse-node-grid interpolated channel kernels and reconstruct F(f)=sum_a exp(1j*w*tau_a)*K_a at the dense bin sub-sample frequencies, and independently evaluate the engine DIRECTLY at those same 506 frequencies (the pre-lever-2 dense path) to get the oracle F_dense(f). Expected result: max over frequencies of |F_interp(f)-F_dense(f)|/|F_dense(f)| < 1e-8. This isolates interpolation error from the RB binning floor (~1e-4) above it and the DD accuracy (~1e-10) below it. F002 discipline: the oracle is the DIRECT dense engine evaluation, NEVER built from the spline under test. Diagnostic: overlay interp vs dense K_a(w) per channel with the log-scale residual beneath, marking the smootherstep transition frequencies 0.5/Delta_j and 4.0/Delta_j and the branch-switch frequency, to expose systematic ringing a scalar worst-case gate could average away.
  - NUMBA ACCURACY/DETERMINISM PRESERVATION GATE (new/extended, lever 1). Setup: a sampled (w,s,gamma) grid spanning the certified domain: w in {0.1,1,10,20,40,50,200,400}, s chosen so w*sqrt(s) in {1,10,30,48}, gamma in {0.0,0.2}, kappa=beta=0 (skip w>500 or w*sqrt(s)>60). Operation: evaluate the numba-accelerated point_mass_g_derivatives and F_op. Expected result: (a) they agree with an INDEPENDENT mpmath reference (mpmath.hyp1f1 with Kummer reconstruction of the s-derivative ladder for the kernel; an mpmath high-precision contour/series evaluation for F_op) to the ORIGINAL tolerance (relative ~1e-10 out to w*sqrt(s)~50, ~1e-6 at the ceiling 60) - i.e. the numba path preserves the pre-numba accuracy, judged against mpmath, NEVER against the numba code itself (F002); (b) repeated calls return bit-identical results (pure function, assertEqual); (c) every F005 CancellationError refusal still fires on the same out-of-certification inputs. Diagnostic: relative-error-vs-(w*sqrt(s)) curve with the 1e-10 and 1e-6 lines marked, confirming the cancellation-law envelope is unchanged by JIT compilation.
  - FEW-MS TIMING GATE (new/updated; owner directive: fast in-build gates only). Setup: the crown 4-image seeded fixture, warm (numba already compiled). Operation: measure warm best-of-5 wall time of the public lnlike on that single config, and separately time the pure _data_term+_norm_term contraction vs the _amplification_coefficients engine call. Expected result: best-of-5 lnlike <= 10 ms on the server (regression ceiling; target is few-ms), AND lnlike still beats lnlike_bruteforce by at least SPEEDUP_MIN (existing gate). Do NOT spec the full brute-force sweep or any hour-scale run. Diagnostic: print the engine-vs-contraction breakdown so a regression pinpoints which lever slipped.
  - CROWN ACCURACY ANCHORS PRESERVED THROUGH THE FAST PATH (must stay green; existing gates re-exercised on the fast path, one eval per path). RB-vs-brute agreement on the crown 4-image config at the ORIGINAL RB_ATOL=1.5 (|lnlike - lnlike_bruteforce| < 1.5, one eval each path); the F->1 zero-noise floor at gamma=kappa=0 stays <= 1e-2 (the fast path must reproduce the F007/F009 template-construction floor, not 'improve' it); MacroMagnificationLimitTestCase stays at relative 7.85e-9 for |F_op| vs the closed form 1/sqrt((1-kappa)**2-gamma**2) at w down to 1e-12 (engine-level, exercises numba tiny-w early-exit; the coarse spline is never invoked at w~1e-12 since that is engine-level not in-band). Expected result: all pass at unchanged tolerances; a NearCuspRegressionPin-style deterministic lnlike value on the near-cusp config still reproduces (verifies the F008 switch fix, kernel reduction and contraction still agree through the fast path).

